# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the two households the rule presses
# Hesh hands in the barns at Haldane's for the harvest. The rule (the residency rule, passed by a show of hands at e1.board) is the
# pressure; Josh Brack and George Orme decide, in written scenes.
@household e1_sallis
name: The Sallises, in the barns
street: haldane_yard
people: hesh
hesh: 1
place: q_yard
members: Arn, Ketti, Davin
taken: 0
portion: 1

@household e1_tesk
name: The Tesks, on the hill
street: haldane_yard
people: hesh
hesh: 1
place: q_hill
members: Tesk, Kel
taken: 0
portion: 1

@fate f.e1_sallis
pressure: has(e1.rule_passed)
subject: household e1_sallis
decider: JOSH
scene: e1.frost.decide, e1.frost.sent, e1.frost.kept
window: 7
who: Ketti
because: the board's rule, passed by a show of hands, says seasonal hands are not residents; at the first frost Josh Brack stands at the pole and says, face by face, who goes up the hill road and who stands on the verge, kept

@fate f.e1_kel
pressure: has(e1.rule_passed)
subject: household e1_tesk
decider: GEORGE
scene: e1.kel.decide, e1.kel.kept, e1.kel.walked
window: 7
taken: yes
who: Kel
because: under the rule any charge is a reason to send a hand up the hill; George Orme says whether the boy is docked and strapped and kept, or walked to the post and sent up barefoot with his boots hung on the nail

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- what the fates leave in the world (the device rule, 2026-10-23)
# A fate is met as a changed place or person, never as a line in a record (world/echo.mjs, tools/echocheck.mjs).
@echo e1.e.kel_stalk
place: q1_barns
when: has(e1.kel_walked)
from: 1
to: 1
tells: fate f.e1_kel
show: absent e1.kel
line: By the fire, Davin Sallis has Kel's split barley stalk and is blowing at it. It makes a noise like a door. Nobody tells him to breathe at it.
sense: e1.stalk

@echo e1.e.kel_boots
place: q_post
when: has(e1.kel_walked)
from: 1
to: 1
tells: fate f.e1_kel
line: Kel Tesk's boots still hang by their laces from the nail on the post, stiff with frost. The barley's gone out of them. The birds had it, or somebody did.
sense: e1.boots

@echo e1.e.sallis_straw
place: q1_barns
when: has(e1.sallis_sent)
from: 1
to: 1
tells: fate f.e1_sallis
show: absent e1.ketti
line: In the end barn the straw is still pressed in the shape of the three of them, a long one and one curled against it and a small one. Ketti's patch cloth hangs on the nail where she left it.
sense: room.cold

@echo e1.e.sallis_stool
place: q_sheaf
when: has(e1.sallis_sent)
from: 2
to: 2
tells: fate f.e1_sallis
show: person e1.arn slump
line: At the far end of the bar Arn Sallis sits with his lad, Davin, grown broad now. There's a third stool beside them with Arn's coat on it, and he moves the coat for nobody.
sense: chair.empty

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- era 1's own senses and loads (shared ones: senses.lwd)
@sense e1.stalk
sound: breath 0.3 near 1.2
caption: a boy blowing at a barley stalk, and no note coming
hold: 0.8

@sense e1.boots
sound: wind 0.3 far 2
caption: wind across the post road
screen: tint #c8d8e8 0.12 2

@sense e1.pole
sound: creak 0.6 near 1.4
sound: thud 0.4 near
caption: the post pole going up on its weight, and the weight hitting the ground
rumble: 0.45 0.1 300

@sense e1.key
sound: latch 0.7 near
caption: a big key turning in an old lock
rumble: 0.3 0.4 260
screen: vignette 0.3 1.6
hold: 1

@sense e1.coin
sound: spoon 0.3 near
caption: a coin dropped into a palm
rumble: 0.05 0.2 80

@sense e1.strap
sound: thud 0.7 near
caption: the strap coming down on a bare back
screen: shake 0.15 0.2
rumble: 0.5 0.3 140

@sense e1.doorpins
sound: creak 0.8 near 1.6
sound: thud 0.7 near
caption: the barn door shrieking off its pins and coming down
rumble: 0.8 0.3 380
screen: shake 0.2 0.3

@load e1.load.bundle
name: The Corleys' bundle
weight: 18
line: Bedding rolled round a pot and a kettle, tied with cord. It's warm from the woman's back and it smells of her children.

@load e1.load.weights
name: The scale's brass weights
weight: 32
